{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308813-modified-banu-haqim-symbol","id":1308813,"title":"Modified Banu Haqim Symbol","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-29T16:13:03-07:00","id":1308813,"title":"Modified Banu Haqim Symbol","content":"In a Discord discussion, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12561_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12561\" data-vbnamecard=\"12561\">Shawarbaaz</a> mentioned that the Arabic writing in the Banu Haqim clan symbol was wrong: even in square script, the letters should be joined together, not isolated. So I tried to make a new version, using proper Kufic square script.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: Don't actually use this one, use the ones from the later post, this one's not very good.</b><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/zv4y3zcv/banu-haqim-star-white.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I'm far from an expert calligrapher, and it shows\u2014a better calligrapher than me would have made it properly square and found a way to connect the lam to the bet\u2014but I hope others find this useful! Feel free to use it for whatever purpose (credit is appreciated but not required).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","user":"Draconis","date":". 04-14-2020, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T20:45:53-07:00","id":1308875,"title":"","content":"Good job Drac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T21:21:59-07:00","id":1331436,"title":"","content":"So I'm apparently a perfectionist and never satisfied :P I made a lot of mistakes in designing the symbol above, and they were annoying me, so I went back and did it over again. Properly, this time.<br /> <br /> If I did everything properly, this should say &quot;Banu Haqim&quot; (or rather <i>Abna' \u0126ekeem</i>) in Kufic square script, four times over. The fun thing about this script is that it was never meant to be particularly legible!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/JDFRX7vz\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/JDFRX7vz/banu-haqim-new-1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/5QFbSdWq\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/5QFbSdWq/banu-haqim-new-2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/t12qXNzP\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/t12qXNzP/banu-haqim-new-3.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> Click the images for larger versions; consider these licensed under Creative Commons Attribution\u2014do whatever you want with them, just give me credit where appropriate. Translation by Shawarbaaz again because my actual Arabic knowledge is lacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T21:23:11-07:00","id":1331437,"title":"","content":"And some versions incorporating the red star background from the Cam book; I ripped the star from the PDF and own no rights to that part.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/Dmt2yZ1C\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/Dmt2yZ1C/banu-haqim-new-red-1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/5XJbLR7L\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/5XJbLR7L/banu-haqim-new-red-2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/PNLXjZvp\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/PNLXjZvp/banu-haqim-new-red-3.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/QH1jB3bj\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/QH1jB3bj/banu-haqim-new-red-4.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T08:34:02-07:00","id":1552075,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Neat! I've integrated it into my Vampire: The Masquerade chronicle as the symbol of the <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/wikis/banu-haqim\" target=\"_blank\">Banu Haqim</a> in general! The <b>V5</b> symbol is the one used by the <i>munafiqun</i></span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Camarilla &quot;Haqimites.&quot;<br /> <br /> Thanks for this... I don't quite know how to give you full credit on my Obsidian Portal page, though. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T16:15:05-07:00","id":1552085,"title":"","content":"Nothing wrong about being a perfectionist on stuff we truly appreciate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T12:04:05-07:00","id":1552110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308813-modified-banu-haqim-symbol?p=1331436#post1331436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm apparently a perfectionist and never satisfied :P I made a lot of mistakes in designing the symbol above, and they were annoying me, so I went back and did it over again. Properly, this time.<br /> <br /> If I did everything properly, this should say &quot;Banu Haqim&quot; (or rather <i>Abna' \u0126ekeem</i>) in Kufic square script, four times over. The fun thing about this script is that it was never meant to be particularly legible!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/JDFRX7vz\" target=\"_blank\"><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/JDFRX7vz/banu-haqim-new-1.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/JDFRX7vz/banu-haqim-new-1.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/JDFRX7vz/banu-haqim-new-1.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/5QFbSdWq\" target=\"_blank\"><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/5QFbSdWq/banu-haqim-new-2.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/5QFbSdWq/banu-haqim-new-2.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/5QFbSdWq/banu-haqim-new-2.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/t12qXNzP\" target=\"_blank\"><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/t12qXNzP/banu-haqim-new-3.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/t12qXNzP/banu-haqim-new-3.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/t12qXNzP/banu-haqim-new-3.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a><br /> <br /> Click the images for larger versions; consider these licensed under Creative Commons Attribution\u2014do whatever you want with them, just give me credit where appropriate. Translation by Shawarbaaz again because my actual Arabic knowledge is lacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>(commenting as an Arabic graduate)<br /> may I ask why you opted for Abn\u0101\u2019 Hak\u012bm instead of Ban\u016b Hak\u012bm? Ban\u016b is what's used more typically for tribes, clans and people. Abn\u0101\u2019 doesn't work the same way, even though it also means sons of Hak\u012bm.<br /> <br /> Another thing is that Hak\u012bm is a legit word in Arabic, meaning &quot;very wise&quot; and it implies philosophical wisdom (including magical and scientific, as I am referring to premodern philosophy which encompassed metaphysics, logic, ethics, mathematics, physics, astronomy, alchemy, medicine, astrology, and theurgy, and many other things) as well as legal wisdom (the wisdom to judge and rule). Haq\u012bm (using the letter q\u0101f \u0642 instead of k\u0101f \u0643), on the other side, does not correspond to any Arabic root I know. I think it's totally fine to switch Haq\u012bm's name for Hak\u012bm seen as it works so well with him being known for his wisdom and authority, but I also like the idea of him being called Haq\u012bm (with q\u0101f) to underline how his name actually originates from some unknown language and it just bears a lucky resemblance to hak\u012bm. That's just my own flavour thing though. It's also totally possible to say that Western vampires messed up the transliteration of the name and it stuck, as it did happen with some Arabic names that were transliterated into Latin in the Middle Ages and in general happens often between languages.<br /> <br /> As for Kufic script not being meant to be legible: the problem is that only a small portion of Arabs in the 7th century CE could read and write, as most of their literature and culture was transmitted orally - much more convenient for semi-nomadic people. Those who could write did so in a sort of shorthand where vowel marks were absent (like in other semitic languages) and 2 or 3 or 4 letters could be represented with the same sign, which can work in Arabic due to some other linguistic factors, also linked, I believe, to the larger semitic language family and how these languages and their dialects manifest local variations. This worked fine until Islam spread to non-Arabs and their grasp of Arabic was not intuitive enough to fill in the gaps as appropriate, so to prevent mistakes in the recitation of the Quran and make things easier overall, other marks were invented to indicate vowels and distinguish letters that were written similarly. So it's not so much that it wasn't meant to be particularly legible, it's just not legible for people who weren't part of the environment where it was devised and functional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 07-06-2025, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T13:50:25-07:00","id":1552113,"title":"","content":"By the time written Arabic appeared, the origin of the name Haq\u012bm or Hak\u012bm would be already lost to time. Probably no vampire involved in defining the written form of the clan name could say for sure how it should be spelled.<br /> <br /> At this point, almost any explanation may be invented on why they chose to use q\u0101f \u0642, and it may have happened at any moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T01:26:59-07:00","id":1552131,"title":"","content":"While Semitic languages do have their variations, the base roots are usually maintained, and written Semitic is 4,500 years old... which depending on which set of VtM lore you chose to go with could easily mean that the distinction isn't so old that whoever started writing it in Arabic was taking a shot in the dark as opposed to just swapping from an older language to a newer one. My own bias a bit here, but early written Hebrew had the same exact h-k-m root for wise significantly earlier than written Arabic, and likewise h-q-m wouldn't make sense (in this context anyway). And even before that, the Semitic letters k and q are not always phonetically the same in a given language; so even from oral sources there were ways within a language to know which consonant was in a root before a given Semitic language started being written down.<br /> <br /> It's also not unheard of (though obviously rare because it would be special to do) for later Semitic languages to maintain an archaic or borrowed spelling specifically to denote something as unique/mysterious/etc.; just as Hermeticus indicated. To me this feels like most likely explanation for the Clan using Haqim as Arabic became a dominate language considering the overall linguistic history of the language family. Despite the wide range of writing systems Semitic languages have used to express rather similar languages (spelling the same thing in Akkadian, Phoenician, and Arabic is going to look far more different than it would likely sound), and the longevity of vampires, it seems very unlikely that the &quot;proper&quot; spelling would have been lost easily. And there aren't that many reasons for &quot;why&quot; to pick from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T01:44:15-07:00","id":1552132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308813-modified-banu-haqim-symbol?p=1552131#post1552131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Semitic languages do have their variations, the base roots are usually maintained, and written Semitic is 4,500 years old... which depending on which set of VtM lore you chose to go with could easily mean that the distinction isn't so old that whoever started writing it in Arabic was taking a shot in the dark as opposed to just swapping from an older language to a newer one. My own bias a bit here, but early written Hebrew had the same exact h-k-m root for wise significantly earlier than written Arabic, and likewise h-q-m wouldn't make sense (in this context anyway). And even before that, the Semitic letters k and q are not always phonetically the same in a given language; so even from oral sources there were ways within a language to know which consonant was in a root before a given Semitic language started being written down.<br /> <br /> It's also not unheard of (though obviously rare because it would be special to do) for later Semitic languages to maintain an archaic or borrowed spelling specifically to denote something as unique/mysterious/etc.; just as Hermeticus indicated. To me this feels like most likely explanation for the Clan using Haqim as Arabic became a dominate language considering the overall linguistic history of the language family. Despite the wide range of writing systems Semitic languages have used to express rather similar languages (spelling the same thing in Akkadian, Phoenician, and Arabic is going to look far more different than it would likely sound), and the longevity of vampires, it seems very unlikely that the &quot;proper&quot; spelling would have been lost easily. And there aren't that many reasons for &quot;why&quot; to pick from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will just say that Sumerian, unlike later Mesopotamian languages, is not a Semitic language. And by their myths we can firmly place them as post-Great Flood in the game's timeline. Hence I would say that yes, if Haqim was a semitic word, the origin could have been retained to some degree, but we don't need to assume it to be semitic at all: it could be from a language spoken by humans before the Flood and unknown after it.<br /> <br /> This goes for all the Antediluvians, incidentally.<br /> <br /> Of course, what you said is also a fine reasoning, and everyone can run it as it goes best with their imagination and at their table. I don't mean to &quot;argue&quot; by giving a response, I'm just exchanging views on different ways one could play this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T03:57:34-07:00","id":1552134,"title":"","content":"My impression is that it's pretty solidly held by most linguists at this point that Sumerian was a language isolate (and it's relation to the Semitic language family is as one of the languages that was blended into the mix of proto-Semitic, esp since the earliest Semitic writing system was based directly on Sumerian cuneiform). It actually makes a lot of sense combined with the game lore that Sumerian would, in the WoD, be something directly descended from an antediluvian language.<br /> <br /> For the sake of clarity, when I said &quot;borrowed&quot; I intended to include non-Semitic languages as a source; like proto-Sumerian as an origin for [Haqim's] name before the Flood. My point was that regardless of the origin of the name (or how close it even was to Haqim/Hakim) the tradition of the Clan (primarily finding it's cultural basis in Fertile Crescent and thus in Semitic language speaking groups) using Haqim because it helps emphasize something special could have dated thousands of years before the codification of Arabic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T04:41:11-07:00","id":1552137,"title":"","content":"It amuses me to imagine that the in-universe person who came up with the glyph wasn\u2019t really familiar with Arabic but most certainly WAS (and remains) Big, Scary and touchy enough that nobody wants to risk fiddling with their design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T07:30:45-07:00","id":1552143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308813-modified-banu-haqim-symbol?p=1552132#post1552132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, what you said is also a fine reasoning, and everyone can run it as it goes best with their imagination and at their table. I don't mean to &quot;argue&quot; by giving a response, I'm just exchanging views on different ways one could play this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're all on the same page, here. I, at least, am more concerned with giving possible explanations for use on the table than arguing which I think is the correct one or something. Even because the most probable explanation is simply that the authors didn't knew their Arabic when making the name.<br /> <br /> My personal point was that regardless of how likely it is that the information wasn't lost, it may have been. Vampires can live a lot, but at any given time most active Kindred are a few centuries old at most, so there wasn't necessarily anyone who knew the Founder's name first hand at the time of its codification in Arabic. Although I just remembered that this is possibly the clan with the greatest number of active (including socially active) Methuselahs ever.<br /> <br /> But I do agree that the name would hardly have been lost so easily. I think the idea that Haq\u012bm's name predates the Semitic languages is a sound one, and personally I prefer to simply change it to Hak\u012bm (regardless of history, I can totally see someone &quot;correcting&quot; the name later on, even if it was originally Haq\u012bm, to capitalize on the meaning).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T08:57:06-07:00","id":1552146,"title":"","content":"Haqim was always an interesting one with two popular origin<br /> 1, he was a warrior-hunter 10.000 years ago who migrated with the herds across the Fertile Crescent and in hsi free time learned to read, write and speak the language of the dead. This attracted the attention of one of Caine's childer - probably Zillah - and moved to the First City<br /> 2, Haqim was the lord of the armies of the First City; as a mortal, Haqim served under the King and Queen of En'esh, Caine/Khayyin lesser known &quot;first generation of kids&quot; but they became evil and cruel, so he attacked them, killed them and used their blood to Embrace himself to be Strong enough to face Caine (the last art not really worked out)<br /> <br /> Both cases the First City is a common element and time to time an obscure and nearly forgotten language the Enochian tend to surface all across the editions - some even say the pures form of the First Language that everyone spoke before God got angry about the whole Tower of Babel thing (or if you want to give it a twist, the closeset that resembles the original First Langaue from Demon: the Fallen)<br /> <br /> I love to go with this ancient language explanation: Caine, the Second, the Thrid and those who are old enouhg from the Fourtgh generation knew and spoke &quot;Enochian&quot; and it is sort of a &quot;progenitor&quot; language from all the other evolved and even the names like Haqim, Arikel, Absimilard, etc are how a modern language could pronounce it, &quot;how it might sounded/written&quot; \u2026 maybe. Sort of. Eh, close enough.&quot;<br /> Not to mention the older Vampires are well aware of the power of Names and just like how the Baali watered down the Children's Names to not to wake them but use their powers the Ancients &quot;hid&quot; their names behind such language barrier<br /> <br /> The re-drawn symbol of yours looks very good!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T11:00:40-07:00","id":1552149,"title":"","content":"Eh, I find the idea of a First Language existing 10 thousand years ago more than a bit jarring. But the idea of an Enochian language from the time of the First City isn't necessarily bad, as it can be a regional language anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T02:56:24-07:00","id":1552192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1308813-modified-banu-haqim-symbol?p=1552146#post1552146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haqim was always an interesting one with two popular origin<br /> 1, he was a warrior-hunter 10.000 years ago who migrated with the herds across the Fertile Crescent and in hsi free time learned to read, write and speak the language of the dead. This attracted the attention of one of Caine's childer - probably Zillah - and moved to the First City<br /> 2, Haqim was the lord of the armies of the First City; as a mortal, Haqim served under the King and Queen of En'esh, Caine/Khayyin lesser known &quot;first generation of kids&quot; but they became evil and cruel, so he attacked them, killed them and used their blood to Embrace himself to be Strong enough to face Caine (the last art not really worked out)<br /> <br /> Both cases the First City is a common element and time to time an obscure and nearly forgotten language the Enochian tend to surface all across the editions - some even say the pures form of the First Language that everyone spoke before God got angry about the whole Tower of Babel thing (or if you want to give it a twist, the closeset that resembles the original First Langaue from Demon: the Fallen)<br /> <br /> I love to go with this ancient language explanation: Caine, the Second, the Thrid and those who are old enouhg from the Fourtgh generation knew and spoke &quot;Enochian&quot; and it is sort of a &quot;progenitor&quot; language from all the other evolved and even the names like Haqim, Arikel, Absimilard, etc are how a modern language could pronounce it, &quot;how it might sounded/written&quot; \u2026 maybe. Sort of. Eh, close enough.&quot;<br /> Not to mention the older Vampires are well aware of the power of Names and just like how the Baali watered down the Children's Names to not to wake them but use their powers the Ancients &quot;hid&quot; their names behind such language barrier<br /> <br /> The re-drawn symbol of yours looks very good!</div> </div> </div> </div> By the look of things those twi possible origins of the mortal Hakim are moderately cross compatible - if he were a hunter gatherer metaphorically headhunted by a vampire (Probably after receiving reports of his interest in the Language of the Dead), brought to the First City as a mortal and allowed to prove his qualities in this very new environment before being taken on as a vampire, then I believe you could fit both takes into the backstory of this character.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}